#: 477620e697df411fa14bacb6014464ff
msgid "Our general advice for images is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-wiki-editing-style-guide.rst:349
#: 4ffb018149934c738b159856c88eac4e
msgid "Keep images as small as possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-wiki-editing-style-guide.rst:353
#: 96202952e2b3482695c9ff610a209b88
msgid "Images are stored on Github, so we need to keep the overall size low. Crop images to the relevant information and reduce image quality where possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-wiki-editing-style-guide.rst:356
#: 40ffec5e06654cfeaba542dccaefade2
msgid "Images in common pages or useful across wikis should be in the root **/images** directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-wiki-editing-style-guide.rst:357
#: 2c1b2b93dfd04146a8c9d1665a810f1e
msgid "Images specific to the wiki can be stored in its **/images** sub directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-wiki-editing-style-guide.rst:359
#: 833d1fbf0d164d9c802a650b736df3d3
msgid "Use captions (\"figure directive\") where possible"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-wiki-editing-style-guide.rst:360
#: 59e08707219347a5bf6113523a28a31a
msgid "Link to the image if it is larger than can be displayed on the page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-wiki-editing-style-guide.rst:361
#: e7fd59f660c24cefab8a71a707408508
msgid "Name the file using all lower case, and underscores between words."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-wiki-editing-style-guide.rst:362
#: a40b3578d39c440d86983eb9c75d4bcb
msgid "Name the file \"descriptively\" so it is easy to find, and possibly reuse. A name like **planner2_flight_screen.jpg** is much more useful than **image1.jpg**."
msgstr ""

